    "structural_insight": "Observational analysis demonstrates that false positives are overwhelmingly unanimous rather than borderline: 91.34% of E0 false positives receive >= 90% phishing votes across the 100 estimators. Traversal paths reveal empirical structural disparity: in E0, 74.0% of trees split on either NoOfOtherSpecialCharsInURL or IsHTTPS in the top two levels, and 47.37% of false-positive decision paths (28,993 / 61,200) traverse both features. This observation is consistent with the empirical disparity between PhiUSIIL benign training data (where 100% lacked query parameters and mean special characters = 1.25) and authentic live web routes that naturally contain multi-level paths and subdomains."
